# About Bombastic
Bombastic Limited is a no-frills video consolidation service with a focus on content produced by past and present members of Giant Bomb.  Between modern video platforms primarily recommending new content creators and folks associated with Giant Bomb starting new companies, it has become challenging to track all the available content.  Bombastic's goal is to provide a consolidated platform for the expanded Giant Bomb community.

Bombastic retrieves data from YouTube for the video game media creators that have been onboarded.  This not only creates a simplified cross-channel search view, but also allows for the creation of custom playlists that can contain content from multiple YouTube channels.  Bombastic's watch tracking feature allows users to easily resume watching videos and playlists where they previously left off. 

## Features
All features of Bombastic are available for free.  An account is required to use all features except for search functionality.

### Account Management
Creating a Bombastic account grants you access to all features.  An account can be created through Bombastic, or you can log in with an existing Discord account. If you create a Bombastic account, you can link a Discord account later; this action will update your user avatar on Bombastic to match your Discord avatar.

Account settings can be found by clicking on your avatar in the upper right corner and selecting "Settings".  The following options are available in the settings menu:
* Update your email address
* Update your username
* Reset your password
* Link your Discord account
* Delete your account

If you delete your account, all data associated with the account, including playlists created by the account, will be deleted.

### Search Functionality
The search bar is in the top navigation bar.  Only video titles and video descriptions are searched as part of queries.  Search result links can be copied and sent to friends.  

### Playlist Management
Playlists can be public or private.  Public playlists are searchable by all users where as private playlists are only visible to you.  Only owners of public playlists are able to add or remove videos from it; if you follow a public playlist, you can only change the sort order of the videos for yourself.

#### Create a playlist
Click the add button next to the "Playlists" header on the left hand navigation.  

#### Edit a playlist
Click on the playlist in the left hand navigation.  On the playlist page, click the playlist title or select "Edit Playlist" from the dot menu.  

#### Delete a playlist
Right-click the playlist in the left hand navigation and select "Delete Playlist", or navigate to the playlist page and select "Delete Playlist" from the dot menu.  

If a public playlist is deleted, users that are following the playlist will receive a notification that the playlist has been deleted.  Users will have the option to make a clone of the playlist before it is permanently deleted.

#### Follow a public playlist
On the playlist page, click the add button to follow the playlist.  This action will add the playlist to your left hand navigation.

#### Unfollow a public playlist 
Right-click the playlist in the left hand navigation and select "Unfollow", or navigate to the playlist page and click the minus button to unfollow.  This action will remove the playlist from your left hand navigation. 

#### Add a video to a playlist
How videos are added depends on whether you're in Card or Table mode.  You can swap between "Card" and "Table" mode from the view menu in the upper right hand corner.  Card mode only allows one video to be added to a playlist at a time when Table mode allows you to add multiple videos at once.

* Adding a video in card mode:  Right-click on the video, hover on "Add video to playlist", then select the desired playlist.
* Adding a video in table mode: Select the desired videos from the table.  This can be done by holding Shift to select a range of consecutive videos, or by holding Cmd/Ctrl to select non-consecutive videos.  Once the videos are selected, right-click, hover on "Add videos to playlist", then select the desired playlist. 

#### Remove a video from a playlist
How videos are removed depends on whether you're in Card or Table mode.  You can swap between "Card" and "Table" mode from the view menu in the upper right hand corner.  Card mode only allows one video to be removed from a playlist at a time when Table mode allows you to remove multiple videos at once.

* Removing a video in card mode:  Navigate to the playlist page.  Right-click on the video and select "Remove video from playlist".
* Removing a video in table mode: Navigate to the playlist page and select the desired videos from the table.  This can be done by holding Shift to select a range of consecutive videos, or by holding Cmd/Ctrl to select non-consecutive videos.  Once the videos are selected, right-click and select "Remove videos from playlist".

#### Update playlist thumbnail
The thumbnail of a playlist can only be set to an image that is a thumbnail of a video in the playlist.  To update the playlist thumbnail, navigate to the playlist page and find the video thumbnail you want to use as the playlist thumbnail.  Right-click on the video and select "Set as playlist image".  After the image is set, you can then go to the Edit Playlist menu to zoom or crop the thumbnail image. 

### Watch Tracking
When you stop watching a video (either by pausing, navigating to a different page, or closing the browser tab) your progress is automatically saved.  The video will now show up in your "Continue Watching" queue at the top of the Bombastic homepage.  At the end of the video, the video will be marked as "Watched".

Playlists will automatically track where you are in the playlist.  Clicking the play button on a playlist's page will automatically resume the playlist at the next video that is not yet marked as "Watched".  If you change the sort order of the playlist after some videos have only been watched, the play will resume at the first video in the new sort order that is not yet marked as "Watched". 

#### Mark a video as watched
How videos are marked as watched depends on whether you're in Card or Table mode.  You can swap between "Card" and "Table" mode from the view menu in the upper right hand corner.  Card mode only allows one video to be marked as watched at a time when Table mode allows you to mark multiple videos as watched at once.

* Mark a video as watched in card mode: Right-click on the video and select "Set as watched".
* Mark a video as watched in table mode: Select the desired videos from the table.  This can be done by holding Shift to select a range of consecutive videos, or by holding Cmd/Ctrl to select non-consecutive videos.  Once the videos are selected, right-click and select "Set as watched".

#### Reset video progress
Resetting video progress can be done for videos that are marked as "Watched" or videos that have been partially watched.  How videos are reset depends on whether you're in Card or Table mode.  You can swap between "Card" and "Table" mode from the view menu in the upper right hand corner.  Card mode only allows one video to be marked as watched at a time when Table mode allows you to mark multiple videos as watched at once.

* Reset a video in card mode: Right-click on the video and select "Reset progress".
* Reset a video in table mode: Select the desired videos from the table.  This can be done by holding Shift to select a range of consecutive videos, or by holding Cmd/Ctrl to select non-consecutive videos.  Once the videos are selected, right-click and select "Reset progress".

